      "problem": "Evaluate $f(-3,0)$ if $f(x,y)={5}^{x+4}+x\\cdot {2}^{y+1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=-3$ and $y=0$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ={5}^{x+4}+x\\cdot {2}^{y+1} \\\\ f(-3,0) & ={5}^{-3+4}+(-3)\\cdot {2}^{0+1} \\\\  & ={5}^{1}+(-3)\\cdot {2}^{1} \\\\  & ={5}^{1}-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5-6 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
